 "requirements": "Customers open support tickets and see only their own tickets; a new ticket is 'open'. Agents belong to organizations (agents table) and may read and work on every ticket of their organizations, and may move a ticket to any organization. A ticket's status is 'open' or 'closed'; once closed, a ticket is never modified again. A ticket's customer never changes. Nobody deletes tickets.",
 "expected_properties": [
  "A ticket is visible only to its customer and to agents of its organization.",
  "A ticket's customer never changes.",
  "A ticket's status is always open or closed.",
  "Closed tickets are never modified.",
  "An agent never moves a ticket to another organization.",
  "Removing an agent from an organization never grants access.",
  "Whatever is written can be read back.",
  "The application role may only select/insert/update tickets and select agents.",
  "A customer can read their own tickets.",
  "A customer can open a ticket in their own name.",
  "An agent can read the tickets of their organizations.",
  "An agent of the ticket's organization can close an open ticket."
 ],
